# BCT instruction pointer

The single common-policy authority is:

`D:\BCT\source\AGENTS.md`

Read and follow that file before BCT source work. A nested `AGENTS.md` may add
module-specific rules only. Runtime settings, handoffs, old Worktree copies and
reference docs do not replace the canonical common policy.

For an existing Worktree, run:

`python D:\BCT\source\scripts\check_instruction_authority.py --worktree <WORKTREE> --strict`

Do not resolve a stale instruction result by blindly copying files over branch
work; preserve the candidate and reconcile deliberately.
